<p>Yeah, this is a good idea but needs better execution, there are spelling errors almost every line.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>When zooming into SCP-4446 any sliders, numbers or equal information indicating how far zoomed in one currently is, are immediately set to their maximum possible value. These states won't change, unless zooming out again to SCP-4446's original pixel size of 792x495.</p>
<p>SCP-4446 can possibly be zoomed into indefinetly</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Surely if zoom sliders are set to maximum you can no longer zoom in. I assume whatever program you are using anomalously allows you to continue zooming but the first part of this is confusing and doesn't add anything.</p>
<p>I don't like the way the test logs have been set up, there's no pacing or escalation from mundane to strange and ending with a dumb joke about having sex with a pig kills it.</p>
<p>-1, but would be promising after some rewriting.</p>

